Recommended implementation

I would actually avoid matching the complete error message because your logs contain:

"Data is not valid: [FedEx rest api error: SYSTEM.UNEXPECTED.ERROR - GENERAL FAILURE {FAILURE_CAUSE}. Please update and try again..]null"

The useful identifiers are:

SYSTEM.UNEXPECTED.ERROR
FedEx was unable to provide any valid address suggestions.
STANDARDIZED.ADDRESS.NOTFOUND
INTERPOLATED.STREET.ADDRESS
STATEORPROVINCECODE.TOO.LONG
INVALID.SUITE.NUMBER

Create a method like this:

private boolean isIgnorableAddressValidationError(
        String endpoint, List<String> errorMessages) {

    if (!ServiceCommonConstants.ADDRESS_VALIDATION_ENDPOINT.equals(endpoint)) {
        return false;
    }

    return errorMessages.stream().anyMatch(errorMessage ->
            errorMessage.contains("SYSTEM.UNEXPECTED.ERROR")
                    || errorMessage.contains(
                            "FedEx was unable to provide any valid address suggestions.")
                    || errorMessage.contains("STANDARDIZED.ADDRESS.NOTFOUND")
                    || errorMessage.contains("INTERPOLATED.STREET.ADDRESS")
                    || errorMessage.contains("STATEORPROVINCECODE.TOO.LONG")
                    || errorMessage.contains("INVALID.SUITE.NUMBER"));
}

Then modify your handleErrorMap():

public Exception handleErrorMap(Throwable throwable, String endpoint) {

    if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {

        List<String> errorMessages =
                extractErrorMessages(ex.getResponseBodyAsString());

        int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();

        if (statusCode == SendFlexErrorConstants.BAD_REQUEST
                && isIgnorableAddressValidationError(endpoint, errorMessages)) {

            log.warn(new LogBuilder()
                    .withReason(ex.getMessage())
                    .withMessage(
                            "SendFlex address validation returned an ignorable validation error")
                    .toString());

            return new ValidationException(
                    "Data is not valid: " + errorMessages,
                    errorMessages.toString());
        }

        return switch (statusCode) {

            case SendFlexErrorConstants.BAD_REQUEST -> {
                log.error(new LogBuilder()
                        .withReason(ex.getMessage())
                        .withStackTrace(ex.getStackTrace())
                        .withMessage("SendFlex API request failed")
                        .toString());

                yield new ValidationException(
                        "Data is not valid: " + errorMessages,
                        errorMessages.toString());
            }

            case SendFlexErrorConstants.UNAUTHORIZED -> {
                log.error(new LogBuilder()
                        .withReason(ex.getMessage())
                        .withStackTrace(ex.getStackTrace())
                        .withMessage("SendFlex API request failed")
                        .toString());

                yield new UnAuthorizedException(
                        "Not authorized request" + errorMessages);
            }

            case SendFlexErrorConstants.NOT_FOUND -> {
                log.error(new LogBuilder()
                        .withReason(ex.getMessage())
                        .withStackTrace(ex.getStackTrace())
                        .withMessage("SendFlex API request failed")
                        .toString());

                yield new ResourceNotFoundException(
                        "Resource is not found: " + errorMessages);
            }

            default -> {
                log.error(new LogBuilder()
                        .withReason(ex.getMessage())
                        .withStackTrace(ex.getStackTrace())
                        .withMessage("SendFlex API request failed")
                        .toString());

                yield new RuntimeException(
                        "Unknown HTTP error occurred: "
                                + ex.getStatusCode()
                                + " - "
                                + errorMessages);
            }
        };

    } else {

        log.atError()
                .log(
                        "Unexpected SendFlex API error occurred: {}",
                        throwable.getMessage(),
                        throwable);

        return new RuntimeException(
                "Unexpected error occurred: "
                        + "sendflex API request failed and it's not WebClientResponseException"
                        + throwable.getMessage()
                        + Arrays.toString(throwable.getStackTrace()));
    }
}

Resulting behavior

For:

STANDARDIZED.ADDRESS.NOTFOUND

the flow will be:

HTTP 400
   ↓
isIgnorableAddressValidationError() = true
   ↓
log.warn()
   ↓
ValidationException
   ↓
validateAddress() catches ValidationException
   ↓
log.atWarn()
   ↓
persist statusCode = null
   ↓
return address validation response

So it doesn't reach the ERROR branch.

But for an unrelated address-validation 400:

SomeOtherSendFlexError

the flow is:

HTTP 400
   ↓
isIgnorableAddressValidationError() = false
   ↓
existing BAD_REQUEST case
   ↓
log.error()

That's what you want based on your clarification.


